# .loom/resync-ignore — paths Loom must not overwrite or delete on resync.
#
# See .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md for the full rule. Each entry below
# pins a deliberate, repo-specific divergence from the upstream rjwalters/loom
# defaults/ tree — a fix landed directly in this repo's installed copy
# because it was not (yet) upstreamed.

# 2am#4345 pin audit (operator ruling 2026-10-15, Q6 option 1): the #5552
# (judge draft exclusion), #5690 (backticked Part-of warning), #5741
# (stale-checks 403 ladder) and #5783 (same-host lease / worktree
# foreign-lease guard) pins are RETIRED -- each fix is upstream (loom#9695
# pr-queue draft filter; loom#8831 merge-pr-refs backticks warning; loom#11867
# REST fallback for the branch-protection read; loom 1b92b8392 ported #5783
# as `loom-daemon lease co-occupancy`). Those files now carry the installed
# v0.19.1160 content, and the dead worktree-foreign-lease-guard helper and its
# test are deleted. The two champion pins below remain: upstream still has
# no title-prefix epic-child source, so both files were RE-PORTED onto current
# upstream (only the #5791/#5837 delta is local) in the same change.

# #5791: `discover_epic_children` (champion-common.md) gained a title-prefix
# containment source -- issues titled "[Epic #N] Phase " count as strong
# evidence even with no phase marker, no native sub-issue link, no epic-body
# task-list entry, and no literal "Epic #N" body phrase. Recurred twice on
# this repo (#5774's and #5784's children) before the fix landed directly in
# the vendored copy. Pin both the fixed file and its new regression test so a
# routine resync cannot silently revert the fix or drop the orphaned test.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
commands/loom/champion-common.md
scripts/tests/test-champion-epic-children-title-prefix.sh

# #5837: the follow-on half of #5791. champion-epic.md's own PER-PHASE queries
# -- "Step 2.75: Pre-Creation Existence Check" and "Phase Progression" ->
# "Detecting Phase Completion" -- still read the phase marker alone, so epic
# #5784's Phase 4 (child #5798, title-prefix only) counted as OPEN=0 CLOSED=0
# and would have been narrated "0 closed / 0 total". Both sites now union a
# phase-scoped `title_prefix_phase_issues()` with the marker source, and the
# zero-children case says "count unavailable" instead of asserting a zero
# (epic #3438's Phase 2 is prose-tracked only and is undetectable by design).
# Pin the fixed file and its new regression test so a routine resync cannot
# silently revert the fix or drop the orphaned test.
# Unpin once the equivalent fix lands in rjwalters/loom's defaults/ tree.
commands/loom/champion-epic.md
scripts/tests/test-champion-epic-phase-progress-title-prefix.sh

# #5967 (and #4558): the post-worktree hook is REPO-OWNED -- Loom never ships
# hooks/post-worktree.sh; it is the documented per-project extension point
# (`uv sync --frozen --extra dev`, now bounded by a timeout). Pinned as the
# explicit declaration .loom/docs/repo-owned-files.md recommends, so neither a
# resync, an explicit --clean, nor the installed-file write guard treats it as
# a vendored Loom copy. Its regression test is repo-owned too. Permanent pin.
hooks/post-worktree.sh
hooks/tests/test-post-worktree.sh
